<title>INDIA: BSE figures of India carry forward trade - April 19.</title>
<headline>BSE figures of India carry forward trade - April 19.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is the latest data, for the top 10 stocks by value, released by the Bombay Stock</p>
<p>Exchange (BSE) for the carry forward or &quot;badla&quot; account ended</p>
<p>April 19</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>SCRIP		  SETTLEMENT  AV BADLA  QTY    VALUE   % BADLA</p>
<p>			 RATE				(RS MLN)</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>State Bank	   295	   0.61     429750  126.78   10.78</p>
<p>Reliance	     280	   0.83     437000  122.36   41.11</p>
<p>Tata Steel	   170	   0.35     572600   97.34   10.74</p>
<p>ITC		    415	   0.70     149800   62.17    8.80</p>
<p>L&amp;T		    220	   0.45     187650   41.28   10.67</p>
<p>Colgate		295	   0.61     122400   36.11   10.78</p>
<p>MTNL		   275	   0.54     127700   35.12   10.24</p>
<p>Sterlite	     280	   0.57	98800   27.66   10.61</p>
<p>Tata Engg	    380	   0.69	69900   26.56    9.47</p>
<p>ACC		   1380	   2.57	19030   26.26    9.71</p>
<p>----------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>The average badla charges work out to 14.35 percent on an</p>
<p>annualised basis in the carry forward account ended April 19.</p>
<p>The average badla takes into account book closure badla.</p>
<p>The following scrips have gone into book closure - Reliance</p>
<p>Industries and Nestle Ltd</p>
